{"id":2568,"date":"2025-07-22T11:15:03","date_gmt":"2025-07-22T16:15:03","guid":{"rendered":"https:\/\/www.arkhamhorror.com\/?post_type=news&#038;p=2568"},"modified":"2025-07-22T11:15:04","modified_gmt":"2025-07-22T16:15:04","slug":"the-twilight-magus-is-available-now","status":"publish","type":"news","link":"https:\/\/www.arkhamhorror.com\/news\/the-twilight-magus-is-available-now\/","title":{"rendered":"The Twilight Magus is Available Now!"},"content":{"rendered":"<div class=\"lazyblock-pull-quote-1F4c25 wp-block-lazyblock-pull-quote\"><blockquote class=\"text-large-small text-sand-white text-center py-16 max-w-xl mx-auto\">\n    <p><p>&#8220;So that&#8217;s my mission, then?&#8221; Sanford said. &#8220;Go to Madrid and kill a god?&#8221;<\/p><\/p>\n    <cite class=\"text-xmedium\"><\/cite>\n<\/blockquote><\/div>\n\n\n<p><em>The Twilight Magus<\/em>&nbsp;by Tim Pratt, published by Aconyte Books, is available now! <\/p>\n\n\n\n<p>Carl Sanford is back, but he is the leader of the Silver Twilight Lodge no more. Driven from Arkham in the aftermath of the events of the Drowned City, <em>The Twilight Magus <\/em>finds Sanford in Europe, scheming for a return to power and influence while also being hunted by old enemies. <\/p>\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-image\">\n<figure class=\"aligncenter size-large is-resized\"><img decoding=\"async\" src=\"https:\/\/cdn.svc.asmodee.net\/production-arkhamhorror\/uploads\/image-converter\/2025\/07\/Twilight-Magus-Release_body_02-823x1024.webp\" alt=\"\" class=\"wp-image-2559\" style=\"width:400px\"\/><\/figure><\/div>\n\n\n<blockquote class=\"wp-block-quote is-layout-flow wp-block-quote-is-layout-flow\">\n<blockquote class=\"wp-block-quote is-layout-flow wp-block-quote-is-layout-flow\">\n<blockquote class=\"wp-block-quote is-layout-flow wp-block-quote-is-layout-flow\">\n<p>Sanford&#8217;s salvation, so the man himself believes, might yet lie in another occult, secret society\u2026 <\/p>\n\n\n\n<p>From the book&#8217;s cover: <\/p>\n\n\n<div class=\"lazyblock-block-quote-Z10mP1V wp-block-lazyblock-block-quote\"><blockquote class=\"text-sand-white text-left px-8 md:pl-16 py-16 space-y-4 max-w-xl mx-auto\">\n    <p><p>Carl Sanford, once the Silver Twilight Lodge\u2019s great leader and now presumed dead, lives in anonymity in Spain, plotting revenge against those who betrayed him. Alone, he calculates his first move to achieve power abroad is by being initiated into the mysterious ancient society called the Red Coterie to secretly take it over. Despite Sanford\u2019s reputation, the Red Coterie demands proof of his occult prowess, sending him on a quest to vanquish The Blood Moon, a reclusive blood magus manipulating humans and monsters alike to achieve their own ends. As Sanford uses every scrap of cunning he possesses to outwit his enemies and prove his worth, old foes from Arkham have discovered his existence and are coming to finish him off once and for all.<\/p><\/p>\n    <cite><\/cite>\n<\/blockquote><\/div>\n\n\n<p>The book is the third in the Carl Sanford series, following on from\u00a0<em><a href=\"https:\/\/www.arkhamhorror.com\/books\/the-ravening-deep\/\">The Ravening Deep<\/a><\/em>\u00a0and\u00a0<a href=\"https:\/\/www.arkhamhorror.com\/books\/herald-of-ruin\/\"><em>Herald of Ruin<\/em><\/a>, also by Tim Pratt. Pick up a copy from your preferred bookseller or find a retailer\u00a0<a href=\"https:\/\/books2read.com\/ARKTheTwilightMagus\">here<\/a>.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p>You can read an excerpt from the book <a href=\"https:\/\/www.arkhamhorror.com\/news\/the-twilight-magus-available-to-pre-order-now\/\">here<\/a>.<\/p>\n<\/blockquote>\n\n\n\n<p><\/p>\n<\/blockquote>\n<\/blockquote>\n","protected":false},"featured_media":2565,"parent":0,"template":"","meta":{"_acf_changed":true},"key-tag":[34,17,32],"class_list":["post-2568","news","type-news","status-publish","has-post-thumbnail","hentry","key-tag-aconyte","key-tag-books","key-tag-novels"],"acf":[],"yoast_head":"<!-- This site is optimized wit